# NOTE: telemetry's Dockerfile uses repo-root-relative COPY paths
# (COPY services/telemetry/...), so its build context is the REPO ROOT — a plain
# services/telemetry/.dockerignore would NOT be honored. BuildKit reads this
# per-Dockerfile ignore file (<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore, next to the
# Dockerfile) instead, whatever the context.
#
# Only services/telemetry/ is COPYed, but exclude secret-shaped + VCS + heavy
# paths across the whole context as defense-in-depth (blacklist form avoids the
# .dockerignore parent-exclusion gotcha). On CI the context is only tracked files
# anyway (gitignored .claude/, env.sh, *.tfvars are never checked out).
.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/node_modules
**/vendor
**/__pycache__
.claude
